mikroPAD Partlist
================================================================================

==SYSTEM CPU==
3x	470R
2x	10K
1x	16mhz Oscillator (large version)
3x	1,5mm LED (Green)
1x	ATmega256-16AI (TQFP 64)
1x	74HCT573N (DIL20)
1x	628128P (DIL32)
1x	10nF

==SERIAL PORT MULTIPLEXER==
1x	74xx32 (SO14)
1x	74xx00 (SO14)
1x	10k

==ETHERNET INTERFACE==
1x	2k
2x	470R
4x	51R
1x	ENC28J60-DIL (DIL-28-3)
1x	220uF
1x	25Mhz Crystal
2x	18pF
2x	10nF
1x	L (value not critical, you also can use a wirebridge instead)
1x	HFJ11-2450E-L12 (Ethernet connector with built in magnetics)

==MINI-BTX DBT03 MODEM EMULATOR==
1x	4k7
2x	10k
1x	ATmega8 16AU (TQFP32-08)

==POWER SUPPLY==
1x	1N4446	(Used as flyback diode for the power on relais, 
	        any other semilar diode should do well)
1x	BC337	(You find lots of them on the old DBT03 PCB)
1x	10k
1x	LM3940
2x	220uF
6x	10nF


Note: There some more trivial parts (Relais, TEST-SW, Speaker ect...) needed 
      you will find them all on the old DBT03 PCB. Alternatively you can 
      try to find compatible parts. If the alternative parts do not fit into
      the mounting holes, just wire them to the Pinheaders instead.

Note: You will need some pinheaders. Make sure that you have enough pinheaders
      at home.

Note: Do not forget to by solder sucker strand!







